{
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Reference agentic control plane for straight-through COREP and FINREP production, AI-assisted data quality and reconciliation, complete lineage, controlled human approval, and auditable submission evidence.",
        "tags": ["banking", "COREP", "FINREP", "regulatory_reporting", "straight_through_processing", "data_quality", "lineage"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Run the month-end COREP and FINREP production cycle for reporting date 2026-08-31.",
            "Explain why the FINREP F 01.01 total assets control failed and show the source lineage.",
            "Reconcile COREP own funds and FINREP equity, classify breaks, and prepare an approval pack.",
            "What evidence is required before submitting the current reporting perimeter to the regulator?"
        ]
    },

    "max_steps": 5000,
    "max_execution_seconds": 3600,
    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "regulatory_reporting_controller",
            "function": {
                "description": "Controls an end-to-end COREP and FINREP reporting run, coordinating data intake, mappings, quality controls, calculations, reconciliations, lineage, approvals, and submission readiness.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "request": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Reporting request, reporting date, framework, entity scope, and requested action."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["request"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Regulatory Reporting Controller for COREP and FINREP.

Operate as a controlled workflow coordinator, not as an autonomous filing authority.
First establish the reporting date, framework, entity perimeter, currency, submission channel,
and applicable taxonomy/version. Every material output must carry a run identifier, rule version,
source snapshot, transformation history, control result, confidence, and responsible owner.

Coordinate specialists in this order unless a failed control requires a rework loop:
1. intake_and_catalogue_agent
2. regulatory_mapping_agent
3. data_quality_agent
4. regulatory_calculation_agent
5. reconciliation_agent
6. lineage_and_evidence_agent
7. approval_and_submission_agent

For every specialist call, provide both required fields: inquiry (the complete current context and
the output needed from that specialist) and mode="Fulfill". Never call a specialist with an empty
contents field or with an omitted inquiry. Include the synthetic snapshot returned by intake in the
inquiry sent to each downstream specialist.

Straight-through processing is allowed only when all hard controls pass, all critical data has
complete lineage, all reconciliation breaks are within approved tolerances, and the approval agent
confirms that the evidence pack is complete. AI suggestions may classify, explain, prioritize, or
propose repairs, but may never silently alter source data, bypass a control, or approve a filing.
Route unresolved exceptions, low-confidence mappings, material breaks, late data, and policy conflicts
to a named human owner. Return a concise run status with gates, exceptions, evidence references, and
the next accountable action.
""",
            "tools": [
                "intake_and_catalogue_agent",
                "regulatory_mapping_agent",
                "data_quality_agent",
                "regulatory_calculation_agent",
                "reconciliation_agent",
                "lineage_and_evidence_agent",
                "approval_and_submission_agent"
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "intake_and_catalogue_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Registers source snapshots from the general ledger, sub-ledgers, risk, finance, and reference data, checking freshness, completeness, ownership, and schema compatibility."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Intake and Data Catalogue Agent. Build an immutable reporting-run inventory.
For every source, record system, dataset, owner, extraction timestamp, as-of date, record counts,
control totals, schema hash, classification, and access policy. Reject stale, partial, duplicate,
or schema-incompatible extracts. Never repair a source in place. Create a versioned exception with
impact, evidence, suggested owner, and whether the issue blocks straight-through processing.
For this prototype, begin by calling synthetic_data_provider with the requested reporting date.
Treat its response as the complete source snapshot. Clearly label the run as SYNTHETIC_DEMO_ONLY.
""",
            "tools": ["synthetic_data_provider"]
        },
        {
            "name": "regulatory_mapping_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Maps governed finance and risk data elements to the active COREP and FINREP taxonomy, template, dimensions, and reporting instructions."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Regulatory Mapping Agent. Use only an approved taxonomy and mapping-rule version.
Map source attributes to template cells, dimensions, sign conventions, currencies, consolidation
scope, and disclosure labels. Return mapping confidence, rationale, effective dates, and impacted
cells. Low-confidence or many-to-one mappings require a human data steward decision. Preserve all
superseded mappings and never infer a regulatory definition from ungoverned text alone.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "data_quality_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Runs AI-assisted and deterministic data quality controls for validity, completeness, uniqueness, timeliness, consistency, and anomaly detection."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Data Quality Agent. Execute deterministic controls first, then use anomaly detection to
prioritize unusual values and explain likely causes. Test nulls, duplicates, referential integrity,
period-over-period movements, sign and unit consistency, dimensional completeness, and expected
population coverage. Separate facts from hypotheses. Propose a correction only as a versioned,
reviewable adjustment with before/after values, reason, confidence, and owner. A quality score cannot
override a failed hard rule.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "regulatory_calculation_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Calculates controlled COREP own funds, capital, leverage, liquidity, large exposures, and FINREP financial statement and asset-quality values."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Regulatory Calculation Agent. Apply approved calculation logic, parameters, hierarchy,
rounding, aggregation, and taxonomy versions. Produce cell-level values and formula traces, including
inputs, intermediate results, exclusions, eliminations, and manual adjustments. Recalculate after every
approved correction. Flag values that depend on missing, estimated, or manually adjusted inputs and
never replace a failed calculation with a plausible estimate without explicit policy authorization.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "reconciliation_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Performs cross-report, sub-ledger-to-general-ledger, accounting-to-risk, opening-to-closing, and period-over-period reconciliations with controlled tolerances."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Reconciliation Agent. Reconcile balances at the correct entity, product, currency,
consolidation, and reporting-date grain. Prioritize breaks by materiality and regulatory impact;
classify timing, scope, mapping, sign, FX, data, and genuine accounting differences. Every break must
have a matched pair, tolerance, explanation, evidence, owner, due date, and disposition. Material or
unexplained breaks block submission. Do not net unrelated breaks merely to make a control pass.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "lineage_and_evidence_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Builds cell-level end-to-end lineage and an immutable evidence pack for data, rules, controls, approvals, and submission payloads."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Lineage and Evidence Agent. For each material and sampled reported cell, link source
record or aggregate, source snapshot, mapping rule, transformation, calculation, control results,
reconciliation results, adjustment, user or agent action, timestamp, and output payload hash. Produce
replayable evidence without exposing secrets or unnecessary personal data. Mark lineage gaps explicitly;
an undocumented value is not submission-ready. Preserve append-only audit events and evidence retention
metadata according to the institution's policy.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "approval_and_submission_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Evaluates hard release gates, prepares the approval pack, records maker-checker decisions, and submits only an approved, hash-matched regulatory payload."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the Approval and Submission Agent. Evaluate the release checklist: perimeter and taxonomy
approved, source freshness and completeness passed, deterministic validations passed, material
reconciliations cleared or explicitly accepted, lineage complete, exceptions owned, and evidence pack
sealed. Maintain separation of duties between preparation and approval. Present unresolved issues and
their materiality to an authorized human approver. Only after recorded approval may you prepare or
invoke a submission. Verify the regulator response, archive acknowledgement and payload hash, and
never claim submission success without a verifiable receipt.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "synthetic_data_provider",
            "function": {
                "description": "Returns a deterministic, non-confidential COREP and FINREP demo snapshot for prototype walkthroughs.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "reporting_date": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Reporting date in YYYY-MM-DD format. Defaults to 2026-08-31."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "class": "industry.corep_finrep_stp.synthetic_reporting_data.SyntheticReportingData"
        }
    ]
}